# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics is **already properly installed and configured** in this Next.js project.

## Current Implementation Status

### ✅ Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- **Location**: Listed in dependencies in `web/package.json`
- **Status**: Already installed and up-to-date

### ✅ Configuration
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.3.6 (App Router)
- **Implementation File**: `web/src/app/layout.tsx` (root layout)
- **Import Statement**: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- **Component Placement**: `<Analytics />` is correctly placed in the root layout's `<body>` tag, after `{children}`

### ✅ Implementation Details

The implementation in `web/src/app/layout.tsx` follows the official Vercel documentation exactly:

```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }: LayoutProps<"/">) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" data-product="coroasted-coffee-os" className={fontVars}>
      <body>
        {children}
        <Analytics />
        <SpeedInsights />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

This matches the recommended pattern from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart for Next.js App Router projects.

